{
  "_comment": "The sample game, and it is ENTIRELY data plus scripts - there is no C++ anywhere in the project that knows this game exists. Adding an eleventh collectible needs no code change: copy a Pickup entity and change its position. GameRules counts the colliders on the Pickup layer rather than assuming a number. Because it is all scripts, it plays the same whether you press Play in the editor or launch the player executable.",
  "_layers": "Player, Pickup and World are collision layer names. Two colliders are only tested against each other when EACH one's collidesWith list includes the other's layer - see engine/include/engine/physics/Collider.h.",
